IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pl-types`
IMPORT `pl-eligibility`
IMPORT `pl-leave`
IMPORT `pl-protection`
IMPORT `pl-payments`
IMPORT `pl-goal`

-- Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from
-- ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1987_129.txt, not from the code.
-- Amounts are made up, except the s 71M maximum ($811.05), the s 30J
-- penalty and the s 71Z fine.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`repeat` n x MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0 THEN EMPTY ELSE x FOLLOWED BY `repeat` (n MINUS 1) x

-- A child born to the person: expected date, date of birth, the day the 36th
-- week would have ended.
GIVEN edd IS A DATE, dob IS A DATE, w36 IS A DATE
GIVETH A Child
`a child due` edd `born` dob `36th week ending` w36 MEANS
    Child OF TRUE, edd, JUST dob, dob, w36, TRUE

-- A child born at term on 1 August 2025 (due then; 36 weeks ended 4 July).
`the August child` MEANS `a child due` (Date 1 8 2025) `born` (Date 1 8 2025) `36th week ending` (Date 4 7 2025)

-- A child taken into permanent care on 1 March 2025.
`the adopted child` MEANS Child OF FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING, Date 1 3 2025, Date 1 3 2025, TRUE

`the mother` MEANS `Carer facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the mother's partner` MEANS `Carer facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an adoptive parent` MEANS `Carer facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 24, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

`no history` MEANS `Leave history` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, 0, 0, 0, 0

-- Payment facts for an employee: ordinary weekly pay, 52 weeks at 1000 and
-- 40 hours each.
GIVEN owp IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment facts`
`employee pay` owp MEANS
    `Payment facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, owp, 0, 0, FALSE, 0, `the maximum weekly rate stated in s 71M`, 23.50, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (`repeat` 52 40), (`repeat` 52 0), (`repeat` 52 1000)

-- A case: child, carer, partner flag, employment since, spouse's test,
-- history.
GIVEN child IS A Child, carer IS A `Carer facts`, spouse IS A BOOLEAN, since IS A DATE, `partner test` IS AN `Employment test`, h IS A `Leave history`
GIVETH A `Parental leave case`
`case` child carer spouse since `partner test` h MEANS
    `Parental leave case` OF child, carer, spouse, JUST (`Employment with the employer` OF since, 30, 30), `partner test`, h, `employee pay` 900, NOTHING

